WEBVTT

00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:04.150
I'm Taniyama Mai,

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:05.980
1st-Year high-schooler.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.320
Yet another strange case
had been brought to SPR.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.650
Someone's friend had been
possessed by a fox.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:17.330
A teacher suddenly says he can
see ghosts, and collapses.

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:21.000
Upon hearing that all of it was
happening at Yuasa High School,

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.410
we went to investigate,

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.670
but the complaints about unexplainable
incidents and accidents increased.

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:27.340
What a mess!

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:29.460
What in the world
is going on here!?

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.340
About three months earlier
at this school, there was an incident

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:35.680
where a girl named Kasai Chiaki-san,
whom it was said could

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:38.010
bend spoons using supernatural powers,

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:40.680
was put upon by unbelieving
teachers, and then,

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.350
I'll curse you to death!

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:48.020
And the strange incidents seem
to have started after that.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:50.690
Kei-sensei stood up for me,

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:52.860
and now the other teachers
look at her with disgust.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:56.450
Why do I have to go through
this sort of thing!?

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.450
For some reason,
I have a bad feeling about this.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.040
I can't help but feel that there's
a great darkness spreading out

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.870
beneath the surface of the events
happening at this school.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:53.150
On sunba nisunba un bazara
un hatta, jaku un ban koku

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:55.480
On dakini shara kyara heigi yaya...

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:00.320
Drive them out, and purify.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:06.160
Please receive my entreaty
in serenity, and grant my wish.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:10.170
Our Father, which art in Heaven,

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:12.830
hallowed be thy name...

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.840
Nothing unusual.

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:24.510
No remarkable changes in temperature
have been recorded, either.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:25.850
Of course there wouldn't be.

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:28.520
There aren't any spirits
in this school.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.520
However, there are events
that are actually taking place.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:35.860
We can't very well stop investigating
until we determine the cause.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:38.610
It's no use, no matter
how long you work at it.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:54.540
Lots of foxfires, burning all
throughout the school building...

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:57.710
Was it just a dream? Or was it...

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:08.890
I can't help but feel uneasy.
I've got a bad feeling about this.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:13.560
I hope everyone hurries up with
their exorcisms, so we can leave.

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:22.240
Kasai-san?

00:04:23.570 --> 00:04:26.240
Wait! Kasai-san!

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:27.080
What?

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.910
Um, did you need anything?

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:30.910
Not really.

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:32.580
Oh...

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.580
Are those people all friends of yours?

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:38.920
It looks like they're all
doing some sort of exorcism.

00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:42.590
Oh, yeah. Monk, Priestess, John-

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:45.260
they're collaborators
as much as friends.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.600
Hara Masako too?

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:52.930
Oh, you do know her.
Masako is famous, and all.

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:57.270
She's on TV a lot.
So, what does she say?

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.940
Are there a lot of evil
spirits in this school?

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:02.940
Uh-uh, just the opposite.
There are none at all.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:06.280
None? Even with all the incidents
that are happening?

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:11.950
Mm-hmm. I'm not sure, myself,
but Masako says she doesn't see any.

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.620
Do you mean, you're able to see them?

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:17.290
No, no. I'm not a spiritualist.

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:19.960
I've never been able
to see them to begin with.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:23.300
What about Shibuya-san?
He's a spiritualist, right?

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:25.300
Naru- I mean,

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:29.640
Mr. Shibuya isn't so much
a spiritualist as a Ghost Hunter.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:31.970
Actually, he appears
to be a yin-yang master.

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:34.980
A yin-yang master? I see.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:36.980
So he's a yin-yang master...

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:39.310
Naru!

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:45.320
Kasai-san...

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.680
To be blunt, there's something
fishy about that girl.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:16.020
She was checking us all out, right?

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:20.360
I don't know that she was checking
you out. Maybe she was just uneasy.

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:24.690
She knows that she's under
suspicion throughout the school.

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:28.360
She probably thinks of us as some
new adversaries, you know?

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:29.280
She wouldn't.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:32.030
Still, how about it?

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:37.040
I heard that this Kasai-san
girl bent spoons before.

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:39.790
Could she even possess PK-LT?

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:43.380
PK-LT?

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.710
I'll explain it, for your sake, Mai.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:50.720
PK-LT is the power to affect living
things through force of will.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:55.060
Supernatural abilities are divided
into two types, ESP and PK.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:57.730
ESP is extra-sensory perception.

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:00.060
It's knowing things that
normal people wouldn't know,

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:02.400
by means of a special ability.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.820
Clairvoyance and telepathy
fall into this category.

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:07.740
On the other hand,
PK is the force of will.

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:11.070
Moving objects by willing
them to move in your head.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:19.080
This is further divided into three
categories: PK-MT, PK-ST, and PK-LT.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:23.420
PK-ST is the power
to affect static targets.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:26.090
Spoon-bending falls into this category.

00:07:26.090 --> 00:07:31.090
PK-MT is the power
to affect moving targets.

00:07:31.090 --> 00:07:36.430
PK-LT, as was mentioned before,
is the power to affect living targets.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:40.100
So, why would you think
that Kasai-san possesses it?

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:42.600
After everything I've said,
you still don't get it?

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:44.270
You're hopeless.

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:46.440
Well, I'm sorry I'm so stupid.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:50.780
What it means is, if she
really did invoke a curse...

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:51.780
A curse!?

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.110
She said so, didn't she?

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:54.620
"I'll curse you to death."

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:56.450
Oh, mm-hmm.

00:07:56.450 --> 00:07:58.120
It's not so much a curse.

00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:01.120
In this case, she's using psychic
abilities to make others suffer.

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:03.120
In other words, PK-LT.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:07.800
I don't believe that the girl has
that much power, myself, though.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:12.220
There's a famous English
psychic named Oliver Davis,

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:16.140
who they say is able to slam a 50-kilo
block of aluminum against the wall,

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:19.810
but the story is,
he can't perform any PK-LT.

00:08:19.810 --> 00:08:23.940
She can't even bend
spoons properly, though.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:30.150
There was a big supernatural
craze when I was a child,

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:33.820
and a lot of kids popped up that
said they could bend spoons,

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:36.160
but ultimately,
most of it was just trickery.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:38.490
Huh? You're that old!?

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.160
Yow!

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:44.170
Be that as it may,

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:49.500
the important thing is that Kasai-san
believed in her own ability.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:54.840
She felt that the attacks on her
from her teachers were unfair.

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:56.430
And then...

00:08:56.430 --> 00:08:58.180
I'll curse you to death!

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:03.180
It was then that the incidents
started to occur.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:07.520
We can't very well ignore that fact.

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:10.530
Something terrible happened!
Yoshino-sensei was in an auto accident,

00:09:10.530 --> 00:09:12.530
and he's been taken to the hospital!

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:25.540
A-as I was driving...

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:28.000
...suddenly, right before my eyes...

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:37.890
It's because of her!
It's because of Kasai Chiaki!

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:41.060
Before I left the school,
I ran into her.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:43.890
She glared at me with this
frightful look on her face.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:47.900
She's cursed me!

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:51.230
She really is trying
to curse me to death!

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:57.910
Is it true?

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:59.570
What do you think, Naru-chan?

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:01.240
I'm still not sure.

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:04.250
But the situation
is only getting worse.

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:06.750
We can't just stand
around with our arms folded.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.750
Let's hurry back.

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:11.920
What's wrong?

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:15.260
For some reason,
I suddenly feel uneasy.

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:18.590
It's you, isn't it?

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:20.600
Cut it out, already!

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:23.010
We'll admit that you have
psychic powers or whatever.

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:26.270
So stop it, already!
We're going crazy!

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:27.940
I-I'm not...

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:32.770
If Yoshino-sensei had died,
you'd be guilty of murder!

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:35.280
Hey, let's lay off of her.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:39.610
If we say too much, we're the ones
who will be cursed next time.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:42.490
What are you girls doing?

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:49.750
Kasai-san?

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:51.630
There those two go again.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:52.960
How disgusting.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:56.960
How can Ubusuna-sensei
stick up for that girl?

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.300
Don't pay them any mind.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.970
You haven't done
anything wrong, after all.

00:11:13.980 --> 00:11:17.940
On sunba nisunba un bazara un hatta

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:21.990
In the Word was life;

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:24.240
and the life was the light of man...

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.990
Naumaku san manda botanan, on dakini

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:32.580
May the kami from all around
come together. Praise be...

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:35.090
On dakini shara kyara heigi
yaya chigi yaya nei

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:37.840
In the Word was life...

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:42.680
Naumaku san manda bazaradan kan!

00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:46.680
They've sure got their
hands full with this one.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:49.350
The track team room, that desk-

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:53.020
they've exorcised every place
that had to do with these incidents,

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:54.810
and yet, still...

00:11:56.020 --> 00:12:01.450
N-nothing's going to pop out
in this room, too, right?

00:12:07.700 --> 00:12:09.700
N-Naru...

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:13.710
I'll make some tea, okay?

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:14.960
Yeah.

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:18.050
Say, Naru,

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:19.710
about Kasai-san...

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:20.720
I don't know yet.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:25.390
That was quick! I mean, there's
something that's been bothering me.

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:28.390
What?

00:12:28.390 --> 00:12:30.060
What's wrong?

00:12:31.730 --> 00:12:33.730
Geez, of all times, a power outage?

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.060
Shh!

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:50.080
N-Naru!

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:52.410
Stay calm. Don't move.

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:09.100
I-it's coming down!

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:13.560
I'm scared! S-somebody, help!

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:17.440
Naumaku san manda bazaradan kan!

00:13:25.450 --> 00:13:29.450
Whew, so it looks like they're finally
started to appear in here, too.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:30.790
Yeah.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.790
Are you okay, Mai?

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:40.130
That woman didn't look at
me even once. Only Naru...

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:41.380
Hey, Mai!

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:43.800
That thing is after Naru!

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:45.130
What?

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:46.130
That woman just now-

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:49.140
she wasn't appearing in the room,
she was appearing to Naru!

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:53.470
Yesterday, I had a dream, where
the school was full of foxfires.

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:56.140
That thing was one of them!

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:59.810
I don't know how I know that,
but it's true!

00:13:59.810 --> 00:14:03.820
That woman's eyes-
those bloodthirsty-looking eyes...

00:14:03.820 --> 00:14:06.990
She was looking only at Naru with them!

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:19.170
What's the matter?
Your eyes are all red.

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:21.630
I was up until morning staring
back at that thing.

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:24.170
That thing? You don't mean...

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:27.840
Mai, your instinct was right.
Last night, it appeared in my room.

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:33.180
I thought it might be bad if
I averted my gaze,

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:35.180
so we spent all night staring
at each other.

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:39.190
Why didn't you call me!?

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:41.860
Well, I was wondering what would happen.

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:44.860
Besides, I thought it would
be wrong to wake you up.

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:47.530
What would you do
if something had happened!?

00:14:47.530 --> 00:14:50.530
If the situation had turned bad,
I would have called.

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:54.540
Never mind. Nothing happened.
Don't worry.

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:59.870
Say, it couldn't be Kasai-san, right?

00:15:01.210 --> 00:15:03.210
I mean, to cast a curse,

00:15:03.210 --> 00:15:06.880
you have to have an incredible amount
of that PK-whatever power, right?

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:12.220
PK-LT. And certainly, to be
able to affect this many people,

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:15.560
it would require quite a lot of power.

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:19.230
Kasai-san wasn't able to bend
that spoon earlier.

00:15:19.230 --> 00:15:24.230
You're right. Moreover, a spirit
appeared to the other victims.

00:15:24.230 --> 00:15:28.240
It doesn't explain it to say that
it's simply her force of will at work.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:33.570
Maybe she's making
straw dolls or something.

00:15:33.570 --> 00:15:36.990
You mean, night after night,
to curse everyone to death with?

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:39.910
That's not an impossible story.

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:45.250
But straw dolls are only supposed to hurt
where the nail is driven in, right?

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:47.920
They do not summon spirits.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:53.260
That's right. Straw dolls don't
cause the haunting of spirits...

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:54.260
Lin!

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:57.930
Yes, there is the possibility.

00:15:57.930 --> 00:15:59.930
What are you talking about?

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:02.940
Why did I not realize it until now?

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:07.270
This is a zuzhou!

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:08.280
A zuzhou?

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:12.610
There's a hex at work
in this school, to curse someone.

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:13.950
Seriously?

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:17.950
But what's the connection between
the zuzhou and the spirits?

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:21.960
A hex placed by driving a nail into
a hitogata, which is like a straw doll,

00:16:21.960 --> 00:16:24.630
was originally derived from
the Yin-yang Tao.

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:27.960
To explain it simply,
so that Mai can understand,

00:16:27.960 --> 00:16:33.300
in the Yin-yang Tao, there's a method
of cursing people called enmi.

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:36.970
It's a hex that uses a hitogata,
or a possession of the one being cursed.

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:41.980
Driving a nail into a straw
doll is one of the enmi arts.

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:46.310
Straw dolls simply convey the hatred
of the one driving the nail.

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:49.320
They don't actually do any harm
to the subject.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:54.660
The hexer, the one performing the curse,
drives a nail into the hitogata,

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:57.320
which calls upon gods or spirits
to deliver a deathcurse.

00:16:57.320 --> 00:16:58.990
A deathcurse?

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:03.330
The gods or spirits accept it, and head
to the subject with the deathcurse.

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:08.670
In other words, by performing
the enmi arts, the hexer employs

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:11.760
gods, spirits, and even demons.

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:17.010
So then, the cursed desk, the hand
that attacked Yoshino-sensei,

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:20.010
and the woman that appeared
out of the ceiling

00:17:20.010 --> 00:17:22.350
were all the work of evil spirits?

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:27.020
Someone has cast an enmi spell
against a person at this school,

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:30.020
and evil spirits are appearing
to the ones being cursed.

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:33.690
The evil spirits don't have enough
power to kill their subjects overnight,

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:36.700
but slowly torment them,
leading them to their deaths.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:40.370
And if these things happen one after
the next throughout the school,

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:44.710
highly-strung people
would be affected, all right.

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:49.380
Yes. An extreme example would
be the girl possessed by a fox.

00:17:53.380 --> 00:17:59.050
And so, that's why the whole school
has been thrown into a panic.

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:01.390
So then, who could have done it?

00:18:01.390 --> 00:18:04.390
Isn't that obvious? It's Kasai-san.

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:06.730
- H-hold on!
- You're right.

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:08.060
Ayako, you too?

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:10.730
After all, she had her
psychic abilities rejected,

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:13.070
and was put on trial over them, right?

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:16.740
Plus, the teacher who stuck up for
her has been put through hell, too.

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:18.410
There those two go again.

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:19.570
How disgusting.

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:23.240
How can Ubusuna-sensei
stick up for that girl?

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:29.080
That's why she said what she did, right?
"I'll curse you to death!"

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:31.420
She's just doing what
she said she would.

00:18:31.420 --> 00:18:33.090
That's not true!

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:36.420
But Yoshino-sensei,
the one who's in the hospital,

00:18:36.420 --> 00:18:39.090
is the ringleader who hauled her
up during the morning assembly.

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:40.090
Naru!

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:43.220
On what grounds do you assert
that it isn't her?

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:46.770
I don't know why, but...

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:53.770
Yeah, it's not anything I can
reason out, I just know it.

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:57.110
Kasai-san is not the culprit.

00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:59.780
It's not Kasai-san! I'm sure of it!

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:07.120
Very well. I'll believe you.

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:08.460
Really?

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:11.250
There's no telling but someone
could die over this.

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:14.460
I know, we can't leave
the zuzhou in place.

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:16.800
Lin and I will search
for the culprit.

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:19.130
I'd like everyone else
to search for the hitogata.

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:21.140
You mean, us?

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:23.470
There are two ways
to break the enmi spell:

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:28.140
Turn the zuzhou back on the hexer,
or burn up the hitogata being used.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:32.150
The hitogata will be buried
somewhere near to the subject.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:34.480
If the culprit goes to this school,

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:37.150
it's highly possible
that it's somewhere here.

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:40.490
"Somewhere"? How big do you
think this place is?

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:42.490
You want us to dig up the whole school?

00:19:42.490 --> 00:19:46.240
In my case, at least,
the culprit buried my hitogata

00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:49.250
sometime after Monday,
when we started the investigation.

00:19:49.500 --> 00:19:52.500
Today is Thursday. You should still
be able to tell where it was dug up.

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:55.170
That may be so, but...

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:57.340
If you don't want to,
you could leave.

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:00.510
I'll do it.

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:14.860
Hold on, Naru, you can't!
They're in class right now.

00:20:14.860 --> 00:20:16.520
Okay?

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:23.860
Oh, it's a roving classroom.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:30.540
Hey, Naru, you can't do that, either.

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:31.870
Here it is.

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:39.550
That's the hitogata?

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:43.880
It's well-made. This doesn't appear
to be for a certain individual,

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:46.890
this is made to curse anyone
who has this desk.

00:20:46.890 --> 00:20:48.560
Probably.

00:20:48.560 --> 00:20:52.230
This seat causes whoever sits
here to have an accident.

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:54.560
That's why we thought that
the desk was cursed,

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:57.230
not the people who sat here.

00:20:57.230 --> 00:20:59.230
The one in the track team room

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:00.900
is probably also not for
a certain individual,

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:03.650
but for the club as a whole.

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:05.660
"Track team"

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:08.580
The floor is concrete.

00:21:08.580 --> 00:21:11.250
Usually, they're buried in
the ground under the floor, right?

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:14.580
Yes. Sometimes, though,
they are put in the ceiling.

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:25.010
Here it is!

00:21:28.600 --> 00:21:30.260
Nice work, Mai.

00:21:30.260 --> 00:21:31.600
Oh, no, not at all.

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:33.600
Sure enough, this is unmistakably enmi.

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:35.940
A cursed desk and the track team.

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:39.610
If we extend these lines out,
we should find the culprit.

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:55.960
It's Masako!

00:23:44.730 --> 00:23:49.400
Next time: File 3,
"The After School Hexer" #3
